            <map to='#7a3e36'>
              <bucket>&quot;(RNathan) Saint-Gilles/Bruxelles, Belgique-Mr. Nathan&apos;s property was seized shortly after the Gestapo arrested him.&quot;</bucket>
            </map>
            <map to='#7a3e36'>
              <bucket>&quot;(SHartveld) Antwerp-After Mr. Hartveld left for the United States, his gallery on rue Otto Venius was renamed Galerie Otto Venius by René van de Broeck to avoid its liquidation as a Jewish business.&quot;</bucket>
            </map>
            <map to='#7a3e36'>
              <bucket>&quot;(U) Unger-After fleeing from Austria, Unger and his family found refuge in Paris. Shortly before their emigration to the United States, Unger deposited all of the family&apos;s movable property at a depot in Pantin, Paris, where they were later seized by M-Aktion agents.&quot;</bucket>
            </map>
            <map to='#7a3e36'>
              <bucket>&quot;(Watson) Watson, N. [Peter]&quot;</bucket>
            </map>
